---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About This Blog" description="How this blog gets written — AI as a tool, not a content mill">
  <h1>About This Blog</h1>

  <p>
    Most of the writing on this site is AI-generated. I want to be upfront about
    that rather than let anyone assume otherwise.
  </p>

  <p>
    Here's how it actually works: I do the build, and I journal progress as it
    happens — notes, photos, half-formed thoughts, whatever comes out after a
    few hours under the car. An AI assistant turns that into a readable post.
    Every post is something I asked for, and every post gets read and corrected
    by me before it goes up. Nothing here is generated on its own, scheduled, or
    published without me having gone through it first.
  </p>

  <p>
    The point of using AI here isn't to churn out content for clicks. It's the
    opposite, really — it's what makes it realistic for me to keep this updated
    at all, given the actual writing isn't the part of this project I want to be
    spending my limited garage time on. Think of it as a very capable editor who
    wasn't there for the greasy knuckles part, not a ghostwriter making things up.
  </p>

  <p>
    If something on this site reads oddly, or gets a technical detail wrong,
    that's on me for not catching it — not the tool. Feel free to flag it.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/">&larr; Back to the journal</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
